  "history": {
    "summary": "Ancaster is one of the oldest European settlements in Upper Canada, established circa 1789 by United Empire Loyalists. The Ancaster Bloody Assizes of 1814 — war treason trials following the War of 1812 — took place here. The Fieldcote Memorial Park and Museum preserves the area's agricultural history. The Old Mill Bistro operates in a building dating to 1832, making it one of the oldest continuously operating mill sites in Canada.",
